@page "/AMS"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject NavigationManager navigationManager

<div class="container">
    <div class="row mb-3 panel">
        <div class="col" >
            <h1>AMS - Application Monitoring System</h1>
            <p>
                This was a work project. My manager suggested I implement a system which would automatically run
                some of
                the daily checks which then had to be specifically run every morning by a member of the team.
            </p>
            <p>This was the design I came up with and implemented.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row mb-3 panel">
        <div class="col" >

            <h2>The Idea</h2>
            <p>
                To implement a website showing the status of various checks that could be added to a database.
                This website could be displayed on a large screen and would update automatically showing changes in
                the status of these checks during the day.
                A summary email was added later which displays the current status of all checks at the time the
                e-mail is sent out.
            </p>

            <p>There are five different check types </p>

            <ul class="list-group " style="width:80%;">
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">Cube Checks - Connects to an SSAS
                    server and retrieves the status of each cube defined.</li>
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">Log Checks - Retrieves the log type
                    checks from the database and searches the log supplied for a
                    success or failure word or phrase - only when log changes.</li>
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">SQL Checks - Retrieves the sql type
                    checks from the database and runs the stored procedure
                    specified.</li>
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">Services Checks - Retrieves the
                    services type checks from the database and checks if the log
                    supplied has been updated within a certain time period e.g. 15 mins. </li>
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">Directory Checks - Retrieves the
                    directory type checks from the database and checks that the
                    directory supplied is empty at a certain time. </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3">
                The webpage displays check types with no issues on the right side of the screen in green and
                displayed all the checks which failed on the left hand side in either red (for failed) or yellow (in
                progress).
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row mb-3 pb-3 panel">
        <div class="col" >
            <h2>The Implementation</h2>
            <br />
            <p>This was entirely written in C# writing to a SQL Server database using VS2015, SQL Server 2014 and
                Team
                Foundation Server 2015. It is currently Live and in use.</p>
            <p>There was a lot involved in this project but the main components were as follows: </p>
            <ul class="list-group" style="width:80%;">
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">A webpage which updates every 5 mins
                    using AJAX showing the status of a set of checks. </li>
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">A database which holds details of
                    each check required so these are soft coded but have a specific
                    check type. It also holds the results of checks run in a log table and tracks progress of each
                    check
                    in an activity table.</li>
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">It updates Performance Counters on
                    the server which can be read by <a
                        href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System_Center_Operations_Manager">SCOM</a>. The counters
                    are
                    set to 0 if the check passes and 1 if they fail.</li>
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">A maintenance page where the codes
                    and checks can be maintained.</li>
                <li class="list-group-item" style="background-color:lightgrey;">It sends out a daily checks email to
                    a distribution list held on the database with a snapshot view
                    as at that time - currently 8:00AM. It holds the status of all checks in one email.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row mb-3">
        <div class="col">
            <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="() => ReturnButton()">Return to home</button>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>


@code {
    private void ReturnButton() => navigationManager!.NavigateTo("/");
}
